OneiOS take23, stack 555b13d (NativeMetal 935c468), patches-555b13d/NativeMetal/0011: the pipelines Core Animation asks its binary
archive for are made in the background, and a counter of what the render server allocates (a diagnostic).
Upstream: none (OneiOS). Needs 0009 (the kept states); applies after 0001-0010.

1. Archive asks. ON with oneios-prewarm=1; off with oneios-prewarm-archive=0 (ONEIOS_PREWARM_ARCHIVE=0).
What: newRenderPipelineStateWithDescriptor:options:... with MTLPipelineOptionFailOnBinaryArchiveMiss ("give me this pipeline only if
it needs no compile") was left alone by 0009 and refused by the runtime (no binary archive here). Now oneiosKeptState answers it from
the kept states when an equal descriptor's state is kept; when none is, the ask is refused as before and a copy of the descriptor
(binaryArchives cleared) is made on a serial utility-QoS queue, after the render server's own asks have been quiet for 100 ms, one
every 4 ms; the state is kept (and recorded in prewarm2.log) by 0009's oneiosKeepState, so the first real use is returned at once
and the next boot's pass makes it too. Each descriptor is queued once a boot; nothing is queued past oneios-prewarm-max.
Why: take22b's iOS log, backboardd, 03:49:08.3-08.5 UTC: 64 "render pipeline refused: ... BinaryArchiveMiss ... compiler untried"
lines in 0.2 s (the log's limit; the count after it is not printed), for fixed_frag_lph_cpf, the path_*, blur, downsample and all the
glass_* functions: Core Animation's own list of the pipelines the system's animations need, asked before any of them is drawn. They
were made later, each at its first use on the render thread (0009's header: 1.3-25 ms each): "an animation never seen before
stutters the first time". The owner asked for every system animation to be compiled ahead; this is Core Animation's list of them.
Risk: low-medium. An archive ask answered with a kept state: Core Animation gets a pipeline where it got nil; the state is the one
its next ask without the option would have got (same key). The background compiles: CPU at utility QoS at the boot (a pipeline is
1-25 ms; 0009's pass already does the same 20 s later). A descriptor that cannot be made fails once a boot (counted).
iOS's log (backboardd): `native-metal: archive asks (so far|at the boot pass's end): A asked, H answered from the kept states, M made in
the background (F failed), N not queued (the K kept states' limit)`.

2. The allocation counter. OFF without oneios-res-log=1 (ONEIOS_RES_LOG=1); backboardd only.
What: newBufferWithLength:, newBufferWithBytes: and newTextureWithDescriptor: of the device are timed; at most every 2 s one line:
`native-metal: res: buffers <16K/<64K/<256K/<1M/more +a/+b/+c/+d/+e in T us (S of 4 ms or more, the longest M us); textures ...`.
Why: take22b, rounds 52-54 (03:57:11-03:57:41 UTC, the "..." menus and the Share sheet of Notes): the kernel's oneios-gpu-memory
says backboardd made +1277, +970 and +889 GPU blobs in 10 s each (28 in a round of scrolling), oneios-gpu-ages that 1246 of them
were under 64 KiB, oneios-gpu-legs that 62 of the 1277 took 8 ms or longer (8 over 33 ms). The kernel cannot say whether they are
buffers or textures, nor which call made them; this line does, for the diagnostic image.
Checked on the PC: applies to 935c468 after 0001-0010 (git apply); the base's build-adreno-metal-plugin.py (UniXNU 8789b8d) edits none
of the lines touched. Not compiled here (no iPhoneOS SDK): the CI is its first compile. Nothing of it has run.
Removable: yes (ONEIOS_METAL_SKIP=archive-asks-made-in-the-background).

